# UI Components

## Overview

AiTrainer implements a modern Android UI using fragments, activities, and custom views. The UI is designed to provide an intuitive fitness experience with workout tracking and guidance.

## Main UI Components

### Fragments
- [app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/fragments/PoseLibraryFragment.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/fragments/PoseLibraryFragment.kt): Displays available exercise poses
- [app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/fragments/DiaryFragment.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/fragments/DiaryFragment.kt): Shows user's workout history and records

### Activities
- [app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/MainActivity.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/MainActivity.kt): Main app container with bottom navigation
- [app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/CameraXLivePreviewActivity.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/CameraXLivePreviewActivity.kt): Camera preview with pose detection
- [app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/result/TrainingResultActivity.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/result/TrainingResultActivity.kt): Displays training session results

### Custom Views
- [app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/CustomTabBarView.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/CustomTabBarView.kt): Custom bottom navigation bar
- [app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/GraphicOverlay.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/GraphicOverlay.kt): Overlay for camera feed with pose visualizations

## UI Navigation Flow

1. Users start at MainActivity with the PoseLibraryFragment displayed
2. From the pose library, users can select an exercise to perform
3. This opens the CameraXLivePreviewActivity for guided workout
4. After completing a workout, users see results in TrainingResultActivity
5. Workout history is recorded and available in DiaryFragment
